d going out to LA and beating a  very good Rams team you know it meant a  lot for their psyche and coming into  Philly a they they know it's gonna be  tough and you know I went back and  looked at that game last year week 10  eagles and falcons won by the eagles 20  for 15 the Eagles had that manhood  approach you know damn hey we're gonna  knock you off the ball you know all the  road graders stopped on that good  football talk you know and they did they  ran the ball for 208 yards when they had  six offensive linemen on the field for  12 snaps they averaged close to five  yards per rush I will guarantee you all  week long the Eagles have been talking  about dominance at the line of scrimmage  they will run the football they will run  it hard they will run it downhill  because they believe that's the way to  beat the Falcons explain to me what goes  on with the Steelers because I said this  15 minutes ago they lead the league in  drama and now you got Le'Veon bells  saying hey if they franchise me then  I'll sit out or retire this is on the  eve of playing the Jags you've had been  not sure if he wants to play or not you  know that you had the James Harrison  situa  I mean there's so much going on here why  why so it's dry I like that damn the  drama staff we got to start keeping that  they leave and you know you're our  coaches every week you guys those guys  crazy because that's all they talk about  is focus focus they focused on your  opponent don't give many bulletin board  material no distractions this week you  know we're three games away from a world  championship and yet guys can't help  themselves nowadays it seems and maybe  because the proliferation of all the  media we now have everyday someone slips  up and you know we take advantage that  but this it's amazing Mike Tomlin has  done just a magnificent job with that  team historically and this is this is  arguably the most talented team in the  playoffs I mean they have incredible  skill players but hey I'm still not  gonna discount those Jacksonville  Jaguars because that defensive line is  big they're tall which makes Ben react  in a different way and get the ball  sailing a little bit like you did in  that first matchup so I I think the  Steelers are terrific football team but  hey I'm not conceding this victory  against the Jaguars to him if I said you  were the quarterbacks coach for the Jags  what would be the first thing you would  do with Blake bortles and the first  thing I would do was coach him hard and  I remember being at Blake's Pro day  and I was very very impressed he could  make every throw his mechanics were very  solid  he has deteriorated mechanically and the  fundamentals of playing the position and  that's where it starts so number one he  needs to be coached hard and I believe  it's a reparation project between his  ears because when you start missing guys  on check downs and stick routes by the  tight end and backs in the flat and easy  throws that coaches call to give you  confidence and you start to miss those  it becomes a problem between the ears it  feels like he's playing for his future  eat each week certainly in the playoffs  now is that perception or do you think  that's reality if he somehow plays well  they advance is he your quarterback next  year if he doesn't play well this  weekend do you think that he's not your  your quarterback of the future it's  gonna be a very difficult decision for  the jaguars to make because the  inconsistencies in his game drive you  crazy there was a stretch this year late  in the season he was playing terrific  football and all of a sudden he just  seems to lose it for stretches in games  and except last week I mean it was they  were fortunate was the Buffalo Bills  because the Bills could not score but  it's gonna be a different animal this  week Blake bortles will happen to play  better and I'm not talking about running  for 88 yards I'm talking about throwing  the football because they're gonna